    "https://esf.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203560": {
      "title": "Research Foundation Senior Clerical Specialist - Office of Research Programs",
      "description": "College of Environmental Science and Forestry\nJob Posting: Research Foundation Senior Clerical Specialist - Office of Research Programs College of Environmental Science and Forestry \n\tJob Posting: Research Foundation Senior Clerical Specialist - Office of Research Programs Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Research Foundation Senior Clerical Specialist - Office of Research Programs Category: Research Foundation Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Office of Research Programs Locations: Syracuse, NY Posted: Aug 11, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 203560 Share About College of Environmental Science and Forestry: Founded in 1911, the State University of New York College of Environmental Science and Forestry (ESF) is the nation's oldest and most respected school dedicated to the study of the environment, developing renewable technologies and building a sustainable future. The ESF main campus is in Syracuse, NY and has regional campuses throughout Central New York and the Adirondack Park. ESF consistently earns high rankings in US News and World Report, Forbes, Peterson's Guide, The Washington Monthly, Princeton Review and other national college guidebooks. Job Description: Title: SeniorClerical Specialist Unit: Office of Research Programs (ORP) Salary: $53,000 - $55,000 annual DOQ Brief description of duties: This position coordinates departmental projects, research administration related initiatives, and program activities by managing schedules, tracking milestones and deliverables, supporting stakeholder communications, monitoring compliance obligations, and organizing project documentation. The role additionally supports office operations through purchasing, reporting, and event coordination activities.. Project Coordination & Administration: Coordinates departmental projects and special initiatives by tracking timelines, deliverables, action items, and reporting requirements. Maintains project plans, status reports, tracking tools, and supporting documentation to ensure projects remain on schedule. Coordinates communications among faculty, staff, campus leadership, the SUNY Research Foundation, and external partners regarding project activities and deadlines. Schedules project meetings, prepares agendas, documents outcomes, and tracks follow-up activities. Assists in gathering, compiling, and organizing data and information for project reports, presentations, and compliance submissions. Tracks progress on departmental initiatives and provide updates to project stakeholders. Supports implementation of process improvement initiatives through documentation, coordination, and follow-up activities. Program & Research Support: Coordinates research administration - related programs, workshops, training sessions, meetings, and campus-wide initiatives. Assists with office level event logistics including scheduling, registration, communications, materials preparation, and post-event follow-up. Assists with research communications initiatives, including website content updates, promotional materials, and outreach efforts. Supports post-award activities through coordination of subrecipient documentation, reporting schedules, and compliance tracking. Compiles participation, activity, and performance data and prepares reports that support program assessment and decision-making. Administration & Office Operations: Provides administrative support to the Assistant Vice President for Research Maintains calendars, schedules appointments and meetings, and coordinates office communications. Processes purchasing transactions, invoices, procurement card documentation, reimbursements, and related records for the RF@ESF general office operations. Maintains office files, databases, records, and departmental documentation. Coordinates student employment activities, including onboarding, scheduling, timekeeping, and record maintenance. Maintains inventory records and assists with tracking office equipment, supplies, and departmental assets. Serves as a primary point of contact for visitors, faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Assists with the development and maintenance of administrative procedures, forms, and workflow documentation. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Minimum of 3 years' progressive experience in an office setting or a combination of higher education and experience.  Advanced skills with complex computer applications (Microsoft products and software, e.g. Outlook, MS Teams, Word, Excel). Highly organized and detail oriented, strong communicator (verbal and written), efficient at managing time, customer focused, technologically savvy, problem solver. Additional Information: In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY-ESF; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY-ESF University Police at 315-470-6667 or by accessing the following web site: https://www.esf.edu/safety/annual-security-reports.php https://www.esf.edu/safety/annual-security-reports.php SUNY ESF is a Smoke and Tobacco Free campus and is dedicated to providing a healthy and safe environment for the entire campus.  For more information you can visit our Tobacco and Smoke Free Policy at https://www.esf.edu/employees/policies/policy-smoking.php As an Equal Opportunity / Affirmative Action Employer, The Research Foundation for SUNY will not discriminate in its employment practices due to an applicant's race, color, creed, religion, sex, pregnancy-related conditions, reproductive health decisions, childbirth or related medical conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, transgender status, age, national origin or ancestry, marital status, familial status, citizenship, physical and mental disability, prior arrest or conviction record, genetic characteristics/genetic information, predisposition or carrier status, domestic violence victim status, military status or service, veteran status, or any other characteristics protected under federal, state or local law. The Research Foundation for The State University of New York offers exceptional benefits such as healthcare, dental, vision, pension plans, competitive pay, generous paid time off, life insurance and long-term disability insurance. The Research Foundation for the State University of New York is not an agency or instrumentality of the State of New York. Employees of the Research Foundation for the State University of New York are not state employees, do not participate in any state retirement system, and do not receive state fringe benefits. The Research Foundation for the State University of New York operates under a contract with The State University of New York and receives no directly appropriated state funding. SUNY-ESF and the Broader Community ESF is a specialized college within the 64-campus SUNY system, and a Carnegie R2 \"High Research Activity\" Institution that consistently earns high rankings in US News and World Report, Forbes, Princeton Review, and other national college guidebooks.  With a total enrollment of about 2,200 undergraduates and 400 graduate students, combined with the immediate proximity of Syracuse University and Upstate Medical University, ESF provides an intimate, small-college atmosphere within a vibrant, large-university setting.  ESF's extended campuses include more than 25,000 acres of forest properties, both close to Syracuse and across the Adirondack Park, which provide numerous opportunities for experiential coursework, research, and public outreach. Located on the eastern edge of the Finger Lakes region, Syracuse is a small city in a rural region offering a diversity of natural and cultural amenities, a low cost of living, and a high quality of life - ranking among the top 10 percent of \"Best Places to Live\" in \"The Places Rated Almanac.\" Syracuse is situated with easy access to New York City, the Adirondack Park, Lake Ontario, and many other points of interest in the eastern United States and Canada. Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application by September 8, 2026 to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Application materials are required to be submitted on-line. Submit a cover letter, a resume, and contact information for three references online. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY ESF 1 Forestry Drive Syracuse, NY 13210"
    },
    "https://esf.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=200401": {
      "title": "Research Foundation Sponsored Programs Assistant I - Office of Research Programs",
      "description": "College of Environmental Science and Forestry\nJob Posting: Research Foundation Sponsored Programs Assistant I - Office of Research Programs College of Environmental Science and Forestry \n\tJob Posting: Research Foundation Sponsored Programs Assistant I - Office of Research Programs Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Research Foundation Sponsored Programs Assistant I - Office of Research Programs Category: Research Foundation Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Office of Research Programs Locations: Syracuse, NY Posted: May 12, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 200401 Share About College of Environmental Science and Forestry: Founded in 1911, the State University of New York College of Environmental Science and Forestry (ESF) is the nation's oldest and most respected school dedicated to the study of the environment, developing renewable technologies and building a sustainable future. The ESF main campus is in Syracuse, NY and has regional campuses throughout Central New York and the Adirondack Park. ESF consistently earns high rankings in US News and World Report, Forbes, Peterson's Guide, The Washington Monthly, Princeton Review and other national college guidebooks. Job Description: Title: Sponsored Programs Assistant I (multiple positions available) Unit: Office of Research Programs (ORP) Salary: $62,500-  $64,500  Annually Commensurate with Qualifications.  Outstanding Benefits Package including comprehensive health and retirement plan options Location: SUNY ESF Campus. Hybrid position possible, depending on experience & qualifications Brief description of duties: Assist SUNY-ESF faculty and staff in the administration of sponsored research contracts and grants.  The duties for this position may include: Aid faculty investigators to develop project budgets and prepare proposal application documents; in accordance with sponsor submission requirements and Research Foundation for SUNY policies Assist ORP staff in the submission of faculty research proposals to federal, state and industry sponsors; Assist and collaborate with faculty and staff with post-award financial and contract administration including account management, expenditure monitoring, project staffing, and partner contracts. Serve as a point of contact between RF and sponsor regarding principal investigator requests or modifications. Assist with sponsor reporting and compliance requirements. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree, or associate degree with 4 years of professional work experience Ability to consistently multitask, solve problems, and work flexibly to ensure success and provide support to colleagues as necessary Service-oriented individual with the ability and desire to work within a team approach and excel in a fast paced, deadline-oriented environment Strong organizational and communication skills Proficient with information systems and Excel spreadsheet software Interest in identifying, researching, and resolving problems, and following through on tasks with moderate direction Skilled in navigating business systems, electronic documents, and sponsors' website Preferred Qualifications: Two or more years of related business experience (e.g. proposal / contract preparation and administration). B.S./B.A. in business, administration, or other relevant field. Experience in a higher education, sponsored program, or contract administration environment Additional Information: In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY-ESF; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY-ESF University Police at 315-470-6667 or by accessing the following web site: https://www.esf.edu/safety/annual-security-reports.php SUNY ESF is a Smoke and Tobacco Free campus and is dedicated to providing a healthy and safe environment for the entire campus.  For more information you can visit our Tobacco and Smoke Free Policy at https://www.esf.edu/employees/policies/policy-smoking.php As an Equal Opportunity / Affirmative Action Employer, The Research Foundation for SUNY will not discriminate in its employment practices due to an applicant's race, color, creed, religion, sex, pregnancy-related conditions, reproductive health decisions, childbirth or related medical conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, transgender status, age, national origin or ancestry, marital status, familial status, citizenship, physical and mental disability, prior arrest or conviction record, genetic characteristics/genetic information, predisposition or carrier status, domestic violence victim status, military status or service, veteran status, or any other characteristics protected under federal, state or local law. The Research Foundation for The State University of New York offers exceptional benefits such as healthcare, dental, vision, pension plans, competitive pay, generous paid time off, life insurance and long-term disability insurance. The Research Foundation for the State University of New York is not an agency or instrumentality of the State of New York. Employees of the Research Foundation for the State University of New York are not state employees, do not participate in any state retirement system, and do not receive state fringe benefits. The Research Foundation for the State University of New York operates under a contract with The State University of New York and receives no directly appropriated state funding. Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application by June 12, 2026 for optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Application materials are required to be submitted on-line. Submit a cover letter, transcript, resume, and contact information for three references online. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY ESF 1 Forestry Drive Syracuse, NY 13210"
    },
    "https://esf.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=185430": {
      "title": "Temporary - Food Service Workers 1, SG-5 Newcomb Campus, Newcomb, NY",
      "description": "College of Environmental Science and Forestry\nJob Posting: Temporary - Food Service Workers 1, SG-5 Newcomb Campus, Newcomb, NY College of Environmental Science and Forestry \n\tJob Posting: Temporary - Food Service Workers 1, SG-5 Newcomb Campus, Newcomb, NY Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Temporary - Food Service Workers 1, SG-5 Newcomb Campus, Newcomb, NY Category: Support Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: AEC Locations: Newcomb, NY Posted: Feb 7, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Temporary Position ID: 185430 Share About College of Environmental Science and Forestry: Founded in 1911, the State University of New York College of Environmental Science and Forestry (ESF) is the nation's oldest and most respected school dedicated to the study of the environment, developing renewable technologies and building a sustainable future. The ESF main campus is in Syracuse, NY and has regional campuses throughout Central New York and the Adirondack Park. ESF consistently earns high rankings in US News and World Report, Forbes, Peterson's Guide, The Washington Monthly, Princeton Review and other national college guidebooks. Job Description: LOCATION/UNIT: Newcomb Campus TITLE/SALARY GRADE: Food Service Workers 1, SG-5 DURATION: Temporary as needed, part-time position (up to 3 months with possible extension) SALARY: $17.17 per hour  (non negotiable) POSITION DESCRIPTION: Assist in the preparation including simple grilling, baking and cooking a variety of foods and serving of all meals.  Maintain kitchen/dining area in compliance with state, county and college health codes.  Clean the facility such as washing all dishes, cleaning kitchen area, wiping down tables and serving area following all meals.  Maintain sanitation standards such as collection of garbage/recycling materials for appropriate disposition.  Checking in and putting up stock. Requirements: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Basic knowledge of cleaning procedures, simple food preparation and proper food storage.  Possess the ability to perform the tasks of the position requiring medium to heavy lifting, understand and follow simple oral and written communication.  Must be able to stand, stoop, and bend for long periods of time. OPERATIONAL NEEDS: Variable hours and days available (e.g. early mornings, days, early evenings and/or weekends), dependent on operational needs.  ESF's Newcomb Campus is a year round field station, with the dining center operating 7 days a week between May and October, and as necessary throughout the remainder of the year.  Flexible scheduling is available. Additional Information: In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY-ESF; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY-ESF University Police at 315-470-6667 or by accessing the following web site: https://www.esf.edu/safety/annual-security-reports.php SUNY ESF is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, age, or any other characteristic protected by law. For more information you can visit our Tobacco and Smoke Free Policy at https://www.esf.edu/employees/policies/policy-smoking.php Application Instructions: APPLICATION DEADLINE: Until positions are filled Approval must be granted by Civil Service prior to filling this position pending clearance of re-deployment roster, transfer list, preferred list, reemployment roster, or placement roster. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY ESF 1 Forestry Drive Syracuse, NY 13210"
    },
    "https://esf.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=184129": {
      "title": "Temporary Food Service Worker 2 (SG9) - Newcomb, NY",
      "description": "College of Environmental Science and Forestry\nJob Posting: Temporary Food Service Worker 2 (SG9) - Newcomb, NY College of Environmental Science and Forestry \n\tJob Posting: Temporary Food Service Worker 2 (SG9) - Newcomb, NY Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Temporary Food Service Worker 2 (SG9) - Newcomb, NY Category: Support Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: AEC Locations: Newcomb, NY Posted: Jan 7, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Temporary Position ID: 184129 Share About College of Environmental Science and Forestry: Founded in 1911, ESF is the nation's oldest and one of the most respected academic institutions dedicated to building a sustainable future and the study of the environment. The College's main campus is in Syracuse, New York and it has regional campuses and field stations throughout Central New York, and in New York's Thousand Islands and Adirondack Mountain regions. ESF consistently earns high academic, research, and sustainability rankings in Forbes, Peterson's Guide, The Princeton Review, The Washington Monthly, US News and World Report, and other national college ratings and guidebooks. Job Description: LOCATION/UNIT:                           Newcomb Campus, Newcomb, NY 12852 TITLE/SALARY GRADE:                Food Service Workers 2, SG-9 DURATION:                                    Temporary appointment, hours range full-time to part time depending on season and demand SALARY: :                                       $21.34 per hour non negotiable POSITION DESCRIPTION: Assist the Cook in staff scheduling, training, food production scheduling and quality assurance. In the absence of the Cook, assign and provide direction to temporary Food Service Worker 1's and student workers in food preparation work In the absence of the Cook, the Food Service Worker 2 will ensure day-to-day operations are maintained Review menu and food production sheets and make necessary adjustments in production directions Ensure planned menu is implemented Issue food supplies and or label foods for production as required. Develop the recipes to assist in defining the quantities required Review proper safety and sanitation procedures with staff Check service areas prior to serving times to ensure all areas meet service standards Take daily inventories of par stock food & supply inventories Complete food category inventory sections as assigned to post weekly inventories Weigh and measure ingredients; prepares and cooks various meats, fish, hot cereals, vegetables, desserts and simple baked goods. Maintain work area in a clean and sanitary condition Requirements: OPERATIONAL NEEDS: Working knowledge of basic food preparation procedures Working knowledge of facility and agency food service procedures Working knowledge of proper storage procedures for food Working knowledge of the basic arithmetic functions of addition, subtraction, multiplication and division Ability to understand and follow oral and written instructions Ability to communicate and exchange information on food service matters Ability to supervise a small staff Basic knowledge of principles and practices of supervision Working knowledge of cleaning procedures and properties of commonly used cleaning substances Ability to perform cleaning requiring medium to heavy effort As assigned, ability to use and manipulate kitchen utensils and equipment Additional Information: In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY-ESF; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY-ESF University Police at 315-470-6667 or by accessing the following web site: https://www.esf.edu/safety/annual-security-reports.php SUNY ESF is a Smoke and Tobacco Free campus and is dedicated to providing a healthy and safe environment for the entire campus.  For more information you can visit our Tobacco and Smoke Free Policy at https://www.esf.edu/employees/policies/policy-smoking.php Application Instructions: APPLICATION PROCEDURE:  Employment application, resume, cover letter and references is required to be submitted on-line at www.esf.edu/hr APPLICATION DEADLINE:    Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Approval must be granted by Civil Service prior to filling this position pending clearance of re-deployment roster, transfer list, preferred list, reemployment roster, or placement roster. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY ESF 1 Forestry Drive Syracuse, NY 13210"
    }
